			<div class="content" id="post-content-3744934">
									

<p>Trying something a bit different on this one: explicitly rejecting the old &quot;SCPs Must Stand on Their Own&quot; wisdom in the most extreme way I can think of (making an SCP that is dependent upon another to make sense). This might get downvoted, but it's an experiment I had to try once.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>SCP-3445 exists in the same universe as <a href="/scp-3519">SCP-3519</a>. Dr. Rory Jones/O5-6 has been receiving automated information updates on SCPs from the Foundation's surviving servers. He's currently editing most object classes to &quot;Uncontained&quot; and saying their current status is unknown because, well, almost everyone is dead.</p>
<p>As for why he's doing this? I don't think he could tell you. Boredom and obligation, maybe.</p>
</div>
